  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anil Kumar Modi vs The State Of Bihar on 10 April, 2019 Author: Ahsanuddin Amanullah Bench: Ahsanuddin Amanullah In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.2120 of 2015 Arising Out of Case No.-19 Year-2011 Thana- Purnia Complaint Case Di Purnia ====================================================== Anil Kumar Modi S/O Late Swarika Prasad Modi@Dwarika Prasad Modi Resident of Gulmarg Market, Bhatta Bazar, Khiru Chowk, Purnea, P.S.- K.Hat, Distt.-Purnea, Bihar ... ... P Versus 1. The State Of Bihar 2. The Principal Secretary, Health Department, Government of Bihar, Pat ... ... Opposite Party/s = = = = = = ======================================= = Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr. Mrigank Mauli with Mr. Prince Kumar Mishra, Advocates For the State : Mr. Ashok Kumar, APP ====================================================== CORAM: HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE AHSANUDDIN AMANULLAH ORAL ORDER 7 10-04-2019 Learned counsel for the petitioner and learned APP for the the State have assisted the Court. 2. The petitioner has moved the Court under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 (hereinafter referred to as the 'Code') for the following relief: \"That this is an application for quashing the order dated 06.02.2014 passed by the Court of Sub- Divisional Magistrate, Purnea in Complaint Case No. B-III-19/11 registered under Sections 16(1)A of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1955 (hereinafter referred to as \"PFA Act\") for reasons of violation of Section 2(ix) (j) and (k) of PFA Act read with Rule 32(b)(2)(iv) and Rule 32A and 37A of the PFA Rules, 1955-refusing to discharge the petitioner on grounds that are non est in the eyes of law and is based on wrong appreciation of the facts and law.\"",
    "facts": "The fee for the same also seems to have been deposited through treasury challan on 01.10.2010. 2. Pursuant to the earlier orders, a counter affidavit has been filed by the opposite party no. 2. 3. The petitioner has moved the Court under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 for the following relief: \"That this is an application for quashing the order dated 06.02.2014 passed by the Court of Sub-Divisional Judicial Magistrate, Purnea in Complaint Case No. B-III-19/11 registered under Sections 16(1)A of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1955 (hereinafter referred to as \"PFA Act\") for reasons of violation of Section 2(ix) (j) and (k) of PFA Act read with Rule 32(b)(2)(iv) and Rule 32A and 37A of the Patna High Court CR.",
